cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite both the article and this repository as below."
type: software
title: "What a digital twin of critical power can report: identifiability limits the individualization of a two-compartment bioenergetic model - a simulation study"
abstract: "Source code, synthetic data, raw outputs and analysis scripts accompanying the manuscript on what a digital twin of critical power can report: structural and practical identifiability of a reduced two-compartment Margaria-Morton model, estimator efficiency against the Cramer-Rao bound (Levenberg-Marquardt, Differential Evolution, physics-informed network), out-of-sample prediction, departures from the generating model, and identifiability under oxygen uptake and time to exhaustion. Supersedes versions 1.0.0 and 2.0.0."
